    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38735" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prolongo</span></b> , āvi, 1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v.</i> [pro-longus],
				<i>to lengthen</i>, <i>prolong</i>,
				<i>extend</i> (late Lat. for prorogo, profero,
			duco): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dies,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Deut. 6, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">iniquitatem suam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Psa. 128, 3</span></i>
			; Hilar. ad loc.; <i><span class="en">id. in Psa. 119,
			13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Aug. Serm. 9, 2</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sermonem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Ezech. 12, 28</span></i>
			.</div>
